blocks.en:
The 109 supervised psychological constructs ( Table 4 ) are selected from established psychometric frameworks to provide broad coverage across five domains of individual variation:
(1) broad personality and vocational interests (24 constructs, including Big Five, HEXACO honesty–humility and emotionality, Short Dark Triad, and Holland’s RIASEC vocational interests);
(2) self-evaluation, interpersonal attachment, and social functioning (22 constructs, such as Rosenberg self-esteem, ECR attachment avoidance, and Interpersonal Reactivity Index empathy facets);
(3) affect, mental health, and wellbeing (22 constructs, including DASS depression, anxiety, and stress, ERQ cognitive reappraisal and expressive suppression, resilience, and life satisfaction);
(4) values, morality, culture, and worldviews (23 constructs, spanning Schwartz’s basic human values, Moral Foundations Questionnaire-2 dimensions, and Hofstede value orientations); and
(5) cognition, self-regulation, and agency (18 constructs, including need for cognition, BIS/BAS drive and reward responsiveness, impulse control, self-efficacy, and locus of control).
All individual-level evaluation sets are strictly disjoint from training data by participant identity where available and by source record otherwise ( § A.1 ).

blocks.zh:
109个受监督的心理结构(表4)是从既定的心理计量框架中选出的,以广泛涵盖5个个人变化领域:
(1) 广泛的个性和职业利益(24个构思,包括大五、HEXACO诚实-谦虚和情感、短黑暗三合会和荷兰RIASEC的职业利益);
(2) 自我评价、人际依恋和社会功能(22个构件,如罗森伯格自尊、ECR依恋避避以及人际反应指数同情方面);
(3) 影响、精神健康和福祉(22个构件,包括DASS抑郁症、焦虑和压力、ERQ认知重新评估和表达抑制、复原力和生活满意度);
(4) 价值观、道德、文化和世界观(23个构件,跨越施瓦茨的基本人类价值、道德基础问卷-2层面和霍夫施泰德价值取向);
(5) 认知、自我调节和机构(18个构件,包括认知、BIS/BAS驱动和奖励响应、冲动控制、自我效能和控制地点的必要性)。
所有个人一级的评价组均严格地与培训数据脱节,只要有参与者身份,或来源记录(第A.1节)。
